# GENERATED by scripts/make_drop_cells.py from P_drop.cells and /storage3/DSIP/rriva/research/fm4tag/experiments/2026-11_dropout/outputs/P_drop_sweep_7120489/results.csv:
# batch sizes = the largest that fit with dropout (sweep peak <= 41 GiB), learning rates unchanged,
# @est = previous estimate / measured throughput ratio + 10%.
#
# The three full-length pretrainings of P_full.cells (P0, P1, P2) again, with dropout 0.1 on every dropout site
# that exists (rriva, 2026-11-16).  Same recipe, lr, seeds (42, 424) and 30 epochs as P_full, so each run is
# paired with its no-dropout twin.
#   p0_d01 = P0: per-object contrastive (T 0.1, lambda 0.4), gradient clipping 1.0
#   p1_d01 = P1: P0 + jet contrastive (weight 1.0, T 0.1) on the aggregator output
#   p2_d01 = P2: jet contrastive only
#
# Dropout 0.1 on:  encoders.global_encoder / encoders.constituents.tracks   layers.0.{attn,ff}_dropout
#                  (layers.0 is the one rowcol block of depth 6: column + row attention and feed-forward)
#                  aggregator.{attn,ff}_dropout   (P1 and P2: the aggregator is trained; P0 never runs it, so
#                  its two aggregator keys are inert there and only keep the three configs identical)
# Not available (no such layer in the code): embedding, residual, projector, pooled-output dropout.
# There is no head in a pretraining.
#
# BATCH SIZE: B_PRE = 12288 as in P_full is the START of the search.  Dropout adds activation memory (the
# baseline peaks were 32.3 GiB P0, 34.1 P2, 40.8 P1 of 44.4), so scripts/dropout_batch_sweep.py finds the largest
# size that fits and scripts/make_drop_cells.py writes P_drop_final.cells with it.  The learning rate is NOT
# changed.  A smaller batch means fewer in-batch negatives for the contrastive losses: say so when comparing.
#
#   sbatch --export=ALL,SWEEP_CELLS=experiments/2026-11_dropout/configs/P_drop.cells,SWEEP_NAMES='p1_d01 p0_d01 p2_d01',SWEEP_TAG=P_drop \
#       --output=<repo>/experiments/2026-11_dropout/outputs/P_drop_sweep_%j.out slurm/dropout_batch_sweep.sh
#   sbatch --dependency=afterok:<sweep job> experiments/2026-11_dropout/slurm/launch_pretrain_drop_stage.sh <abs path of the P_drop_sweep_<id> dir>
p0_d01  arm=pretrain encoders=rowcol_concat_v0 chunk_size=512 datamodule.batch_size=12288 optimizer.lr=1e-3 encoders.global_encoder.layers.0.attn_dropout=0.1 encoders.global_encoder.layers.0.ff_dropout=0.1 encoders.constituents.tracks.layers.0.attn_dropout=0.1 encoders.constituents.tracks.layers.0.ff_dropout=0.1 aggregator.attn_dropout=0.1 aggregator.ff_dropout=0.1 @est=7350
p1_d01  arm=pretrain encoders=rowcol_concat_v0 chunk_size=512 datamodule.batch_size=10752 optimizer.lr=1e-3 pretrain.loss_weights.jet_contrastive=1.0 pretrain.jet_contrastive_loss.temperature=0.1 encoders.global_encoder.layers.0.attn_dropout=0.1 encoders.global_encoder.layers.0.ff_dropout=0.1 encoders.constituents.tracks.layers.0.attn_dropout=0.1 encoders.constituents.tracks.layers.0.ff_dropout=0.1 aggregator.attn_dropout=0.1 aggregator.ff_dropout=0.1 @est=10340
p2_d01  arm=pretrain encoders=rowcol_concat_v0 chunk_size=512 datamodule.batch_size=12288 optimizer.lr=1e-3 pretrain.loss_weights.contrastive=0.0 pretrain.loss_weights.jet_contrastive=1.0 pretrain.jet_contrastive_loss.temperature=0.1 encoders.global_encoder.layers.0.attn_dropout=0.1 encoders.global_encoder.layers.0.ff_dropout=0.1 encoders.constituents.tracks.layers.0.attn_dropout=0.1 encoders.constituents.tracks.layers.0.ff_dropout=0.1 aggregator.attn_dropout=0.1 aggregator.ff_dropout=0.1 @est=7940
